</section>

<section id="queue-wait-analysis">
  <h2>Queue Length & Waiting Time Analysis</h2>
  <p class="lead">Customer experience risk is concentrated in station-level bottlenecks rather than broad location-type differences. The highest average wait cell is {html.escape(str(worst_wait_loc_time[0]))} / {html.escape(str(worst_wait_loc_time[1]))} at {fmt(wait_heat.loc[worst_wait_loc_time],2)} minutes. Average queue length is nearly flat by time slot, but station segments show local hotspots.</p>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['wait_heat']}</div>
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['traffic_wait_heat']}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['top_wait']}</div>
    <div>{html_table(fmt_top_wait, None)}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="takeaways">
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Wait times are uniform at aggregate level.</strong> Peak average wait is {fmt(peak['Avg_wait_min'],2)} minutes; off-peak is {fmt(off['Avg_wait_min'],2)} minutes.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Worst observed station segment.</strong> {html.escape(top_wait.iloc[0]['Station / Location'])} has {fmt(top_wait.iloc[0]['Avg_wait_min'],2)} average wait and {fmt(top_wait.iloc[0]['P90_wait_min'],1)} P90 wait.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Reward penalizes waits.</strong> Waiting time correlates {corr.loc['waiting_time','optimization_reward']:.3f} with optimization reward, supporting queue mitigation as a high-value lever.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="energy-grid-load">
  <h2>Energy Consumption & Grid Load Patterns</h2>
  <p class="lead">Session energy is stable across location and time segments, so grid stress is mainly a function of simultaneous demand/load timing rather than larger per-session charging volumes. Peak periods have the clearest grid load exposure.</p>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['load_heat']}</div>
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['vehicle_energy']}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="takeaways">
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Peak load step-change.</strong> Peak mean load is {fmt(peak['Mean_load_kW'],1)} kW, compared with {fmt(off['Mean_load_kW'],1)} kW off-peak.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Daily variation is secondary.</strong> The day/time matrix shows the same broad load pattern across all weekdays present in the data.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Energy per session is consistent.</strong> Average energy stays near {fmt(overall['avg_energy'],1)} kWh, making scheduling and load balancing more important than vehicle mix alone.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="renewable-pricing">
  <h2>Renewable Energy Integration & Dynamic Pricing</h2>
  <p class="lead">Renewable energy ratio deserves prominent operating attention: it is higher in off-peak periods and is strongly positively associated with optimization reward (correlation {corr.loc['renewable_energy_ratio','optimization_reward']:.3f}). Electricity price, however, is effectively flat across demand conditions in this dataset.</p>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['renew_heat']}</div>
    <div class="chart-card">{charts['price_scatter']}</div>
  </div>
  <h3>Weather Segmentation</h3>
  {html_table(fmt_weather, 'Weather')}
