    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Off-peak is greener.</strong> Off-peak renewable ratio is {pct(off['Renewable_ratio'])}; peak is {pct(peak['Renewable_ratio'])}.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Price is not a demand signal.</strong> Peak average price is {fmt(peak['Avg_price'],2)} versus {fmt(off['Avg_price'],2)} off-peak, a difference of {fmt(price_delta,2)}.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Optimization reward tracks sustainability.</strong> Peak reward is {fmt(peak['Mean_reward'],2)}, compared with {fmt(off['Mean_reward'],2)} off-peak.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="vehicle-charging-behavior">
  <h2>Vehicle Charging Behavior & Session Profiles</h2>
  <p class="lead">The observed fleet is evenly split among Car, Bus, and Two-Wheeler sessions. Session energy, final SOC, and wait times are similar by vehicle type, so operational policies can be location/time based without heavy vehicle-type exception handling.</p>
  {html_table(fmt_vehicle, 'Vehicle Type')}
  <div class="takeaways">
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Balanced fleet mix.</strong> Car sessions are {vehicle.loc['Car','Sessions']:,}; Bus sessions are {vehicle.loc['Bus','Sessions']:,}; Two-Wheeler sessions are {vehicle.loc['Two-Wheeler','Sessions']:,}.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Bus energy is highest by a narrow margin.</strong> Bus average energy is {fmt(vehicle.loc['Bus','Avg_energy_kWh'],2)} kWh.</div>
    <div class="takeaway"><strong>Priority mix is stable.</strong> High-priority share ranges from {vehicle['High_priority_pct'].min():.1f}% to {vehicle['High_priority_pct'].max():.1f}% across vehicle types.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="optimization-recommendations">
  <h2>Optimization Insights & Recommendations</h2>
  <p class="lead">The optimization strategy should combine peak load reduction, local queue hotspot relief, and green-time incentives. These recommendations are grounded in observed data patterns and avoid extrapolating beyond the CSV.</p>
  <div class="rec-grid">
    <div class="rec"><h3><span class="tag red">Queue</span> Add targeted bottleneck controls</h3><ul><li>Prioritize operational review at {html.escape(top_wait.iloc[0]['Station / Location'])}, {html.escape(top_wait.iloc[1]['Station / Location'])}, and {html.escape(top_wait.iloc[2]['Station / Location'])}, the highest average-wait station/location segments.</li><li>Use reservation pacing or dispatch guidance when queue length reaches local thresholds, because aggregate queue length is flat but station-level wait hotspots persist.</li><li>Monitor P90 wait, not only mean wait, because customer pain emerges at tail wait times.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="rec"><h3><span class="tag orange">Load</span> Shift flexible sessions out of peak</h3><ul><li>Peak mean load exceeds off-peak by {fmt(peak_load_delta,1)} kW; use app prompts, managed charging, and fleet scheduling to move flexible sessions to off-peak windows.</li><li>Focus load balancing on time slot first, then station segment, because location-type differences are small compared with the peak/off-peak load gap.</li><li>Use station demand ranking to sequence capacity expansion at high-demand segments such as {html.escape(top_demand.iloc[0]['Station / Location'])}.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="rec"><h3><span class="tag green">Renewables</span> Incentivize green charging windows</h3><ul><li>Promote off-peak charging as the default green option: off-peak renewable ratio is {pct(off['Renewable_ratio'])}, versus {pct(peak['Renewable_ratio'])} in peak periods.</li><li>Use weather/time renewable ratio monitoring to publish “green charging” prompts when renewable availability is strongest.</li><li>Pair renewable-heavy windows with queue-aware scheduling so sustainability gains do not create new local waiting bottlenecks.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="rec"><h3><span class="tag">Pricing</span> Make dynamic pricing operational</h3><ul><li>The observed peak/off-peak price difference is only {fmt(price_delta,2)}, while peak reward is {fmt(peak_reward_delta,2)} lower than off-peak; revise tariffs to reflect grid stress.</li><li>Offer off-peak or high-renewable discounts and peak surcharges for non-urgent charging, while protecting high-priority sessions.</li><li>Track conversion: measure whether price changes reduce peak demand and improve optimization reward without increasing average wait.</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="methodology">
  <h2>Methodology & Data Integrity Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Primary source: <code>/app/benchmark/data.csv</code>; dataset contains {overall['sessions']:,} rows and {len(df.columns)} columns with no missing values detected.</li>
